================================================================
THRESHOLD THR = 2/7
================================================================
(a) single-run SCALE INVARIANCE (mu_thr({0,g,..,(k-1)g}) = mu_thr(consec)):
    k= 4: consec mu_thr =            19/21 = 0.90476  scale-invariant: True
    k= 5: consec mu_thr =             9/14 = 0.64286  scale-invariant: True
    k= 6: consec mu_thr =              4/7 = 0.57143  scale-invariant: True
    k= 7: consec mu_thr =           83/210 = 0.39524  scale-invariant: True
    k= 8: consec mu_thr =          163/490 = 0.33265  scale-invariant: True
    k= 9: consec mu_thr =          277/980 = 0.28265  scale-invariant: True
    k=10: consec mu_thr =         557/2205 = 0.25261  scale-invariant: True
  => single runs scale-invariant at THR=2/7: YES

(b) does CONSECUTIVE minimize mu_thr among single-block (bounded full runs)?
    compare consec to all k-subsets of {0..k+2} that are SINGLE runs (no
    interior hole, i.e. {a,a+1,...}); trivially consec is the only full run,
    so we instead report consec vs the bounded-shape MIN (perforation allowed):
    k= 7: consec=0.39524  bounded-min=0.37143 at (0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8)  perforation beats consec
    k= 8: consec=0.33265  bounded-min=0.32273 at (0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 11)  perforation beats consec
    k= 9: consec=0.28265  bounded-min=0.22313 at (0, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 12)  perforation beats consec
    k=10: consec=0.25261  bounded-min=0.18302 at (0, 1, 2, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13)  perforation beats consec

